{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "KGrbdPa",
  "isInstrument": true,
  "explanation": "KGrbdPa — a feature-for-feature model of the Moog Grandmother semi-modular analog synthesizer, built from a cover-to-cover read of the Grandmother User's Manual (signal-flow page, every module, the patch-point index, the Global Settings, the MIDI chart and the 14 factory patch sheets). Two band-limited VCOs (triangle / saw / square / narrow pulse, 32'-2', hard sync, linear FM, PWM), white noise, a 3-channel mixer that overdrives, the 4-pole 24 dB Moog ladder filter with self-oscillation and 1:2 / 1:1 keyboard tracking, a 1-pole high-pass filter, a bipolar attenuator, a 4-point mult, the ADSR with +/- outputs, the modulation oscillator with Sample & Hold, the VCA with ENV / KB RLS / DRONE modes, and a two-spring reverb tank. The whole 41-point patch bay is live: drag cables between any output and any input (inputs replace their normalled connection exactly like the hardware). Left-hand controller with pitch/mod wheels, glide (LCR / LCT / exponential, legato, gated), keyboard octave and transpose; arpeggiator (ORDR / FWD-BKWD / RNDM, 1-3 octaves, HOLD) and a 3 x 256-step sequencer with REC, REST, TIE, ACCENT and live overwrite; internal / tap / host-tempo clock with the 24 note divisions, CLOCK IN / ON-OFF IN / RESET IN / CLOCK OUT. 78 controls: the knobs and wheels are real DAW parameters, switches and the patch bay are packed into the remaining host slots. The 14 manual patch sheets are included.",
